"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n\n<head>\n  <base target=\"_top\">\n</head>\n\n<body>\n  <div class=\"fep-events\">\n    <div class=\"event-filters mb-4\">\n      <div class=\"input-group mb-3\">\n        <div class=\"input-group-prepend mr-2\">\n          <span class=\"input-group-text\">Filters</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"btn-group-toggle event-type-selector\" data-toggle=\"buttons\">\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-free\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">Free        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-general-public\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">General Public        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-hybrid\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">Hybrid        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-service-provider\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">Service Provider        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-service-providers\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">Service Providers        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-virtual\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">Virtual        </label>\n                  </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-providers event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Your Clients Are Already Asking AI About Money: What Financial Coaches Need to Know, Use, and Protect</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Thursday October 15, 2026 10:00 AM - 11:00 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          Artificial intelligence is already changing how clients search for financial answers, make decisions, compare options, and seek support. This session helps providers understand how clients are using AI, where AI can responsibly support coaching practice, and what risks must be carefully managed.<p>Participants will examine how clients may already be using AI for budgeting, credit, debt, savings, benefits, housing questions, financial decision-making, and difficult money conversations and explore responsible ways practitioners can use AI for preparation, education, documentation support, reflection, role-play, and follow-up.<br></p><p>The session also covers key guardrails related to privacy, accuracy, bias, over-reliance, ethical<br>boundaries, and client safety, and reaffirms what AI cannot replicate: trust, empathy, cultural context, professional judgment, motivation, and accountability. </p><p>Participants will leave with a practical framework for becoming AI-ready practitioners while protecting the human touch that makes financial coaching transformational.</p>Registration required.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://everyoneiswelcome.app.neoncrm.com/forms/your-clients-are-already-asking-ai-about-money-registration?event=601\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         Service Providers      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-provider event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">From Statewide to Personal: A Webinar on the Power of Customized College and Career Outreach</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday October 21, 2026 11:00 AM - 12:00 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          When it comes to post-high school planning, students need personalized information about the full range of possible pathways, delivered by people they know and trust. On October 21, join the Washington Student Achievement Council (WSAC) to see how one pilot project is delivering on that insight.<p>In this one-hour webinar, WSAC will:</p><ul><li>share new research on the benefits of a regionalized college access chatbot, alongside findings on the most common pathways students take after high school.</li><li>show how small customizations, like tailoring a chatbot’s branding or sharing local event details, make information resonate with students.</li><li>connect customized messaging to improved FAFSA completion.</li></ul><p>Attendees will also hear directly from school and community-based organization partners who worked with WSAC to regionalize the college access chatbot.</p><p>If you engage in college outreach in a school, a community organization, or a state agency, and you want practical tools to help you connect with students and families, then you won’t want to miss this webinar.</p>Registration required.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://wsac-wa-gov.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_LkGnyMqLQsmUDZuGVOUx-Q?_x_zm_rhtaid=542&amp;amp;_x_zm_rtaid=VrKpUc07S3mdZ4cP6Nh3nA.1791328169692.3c21a11059f3b2d35c008f42aeac23a1&amp;amp;utm_medium=email&amp;amp;utm_source=WSAC#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         Service Provider      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-provider event-free event-hybrid\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\"> Washington Financial Coaching Network</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Hybrid</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday October 28, 2026 2:00 PM - 3:00 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          A peer-learningcommunity for financial coaches and navigators across the state. Held on the4th Wednesday of each month, the meeting provides a collaborative space to:<ul><li>Share     Best Practices: Discuss effective coaching techniques, program strategies,     and client engagement tools.</li></ul><ul><li>Resource     Sharing: Exchange up-to-date information on local community resources,     financial products, and social services that support     low-to-moderate-income residents.</li></ul><ul><li>Peer     Support &amp; Collaboration: Build professional connections, troubleshoot     client challenges with fellow practitioners, and reduce isolation among     coaches across non-profit, housing, and social service agencies.</li></ul><ul><li>Skill     Building: Stay informed on emerging trends in financial empowerment,     consumer protection, and state-level economic resources.</li></ul><p> Registration Required.</p><br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://register.gotowebinar.com/register/832114149467688032\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        Service Provider      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-provider event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">FEPPP Webinar: Betting It All - Talking About Youth Problem Gambling</span><span class=\"ml-3\"> Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\"> Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday October 28, 2026 4:00 PM - 5:30 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          The landscape of legal gambling has changed drastically in the last decade, leading to an increase in problem gambling around the United States. This professional development aims to help educators feel up to speed and prepared to identify and talk about problem gambling behavior with teens and adolescents. Topics will include games versus gambling, sports betting, prediction markets, and characteristics of problem gambling behavior. Participants will receive a list of free, reviewed lessons and activities around gambling. <br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://survey.alchemer.com/s3/9027962/FEPPP-Webinar-Betting-It-All\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         Service Provider      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">NCLC Student Loan Webinar Series: Resolving Common Student Loan Problems &amp; Other FAQs</span><span class=\"ml-3\"> Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\"> Free </span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Thursday November 5, 2026 10:00 AM - 11:30 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          In 2026, the National Consumer Law Center will be offering a five-part training series for financial counselors, coaches, and other professionals to learn more about the ins and outs of borrowers’ student loan repayment options, how to help borrowers with loans in default get their loans back into good standing and avoid collection, cancellation programs, and more. The training series will provide up-to-date information on how to help borrowers with common problems and break down what upcoming legal changes mean for the student loan borrowers you work with.<p>This series will be designed for beginners and more experienced folks alike to level up on their student loan knowledge.</p><ul><li>Session 1: January 29, 2026 from 10:00-11:30am The Ins and Outs of Student Loan Basics</li><li>Session 2: February 26, 2026 from  10:00-11:30am  Default &amp; Debt Collection</li><li>Session 3: May 7, 2026 from  10:00-11:30am  Cancellation &amp; Forgiveness Options</li><li>Session 4: August 20, 2026 from  10:00-11:30am  Understanding Repayment Options</li><li>Session 5: November 5, 2026 from  10:00-11:30am  Resolving Common Student Loan Problems &amp; Other FAQs</li></ul><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://us02web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_4cqDGmx1Ssy1UDlgBFLO3w#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-providers  event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Washington State Health Care Authority: Trauma-informed Care for Career Services Series - Part 1</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\"></span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday November 17, 2026 8:30 AM - 10:00 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          The Washington State Health Care Authority (HCA) Foundational Community Supports (FCS) team invite you to join them and Rutgers Department of Psychiatric Rehabilitation and Counseling Professions for a four-part series on Trauma-Informed Care (TIC). <p>This four-part webinar series will explore how trauma can affect a person’s experience with career services, looking for work, and being successful on the job. We’ll talk about what trauma can look like in everyday interactions and how providers can respond in ways that build trust, safety, and connection.</p><p>The series will focus on practical strategies that providers can use in supported employment, including job development, placement, coaching, and retention. We’ll also look at how trauma can affect workplace skills, communication, stress, and job success. Participants will be introduced to tools such as cognitive restructuring that can help individuals work through thoughts and challenges that may get in the way of their employment goals. Attendees will leave each webinar with practical ideas they can use with the people they support.</p><p>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://rutgers.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_aMT_WnpBST2AsgC3HQkwpA#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         Service Providers      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">WSAC Financial Aid Webinar</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday November 17, 2026 5:30 PM - 6:30 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          This session is offered in English and Spanish / esta presentación está disponible en inglés y español.<br><br>Join the 12th Year Campaign to learn more about financial aid and take your first step creating your StudentAid.gov account (FSA ID) or WASFA account at this event.  Please only use your initials instead of your full first and last name when you register. <br><br> Únase a la campaña del duodécimo año para obtener más información sobre la ayuda financiera y dé el primer paso para crear su FSA ID o cuenta WASFA en este evento.  Utilice únicamente sus iniciales en lugar de su nombre y apellido cuando se registre.  <br><br>Registration required.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://wsac-wa-gov.zoom.us/meeting/register/7Rkfcjg1ThadFs2XuFpYjQ#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-provider event-free event-hybrid\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\"> Washington Financial Coaching Network</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Hybrid</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday November 25, 2026 2:00 PM - 3:00 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          A peer-learningcommunity for financial coaches and navigators across the state. Held on the4th Wednesday of each month, the meeting provides a collaborative space to:<ul><li>Share     Best Practices: Discuss effective coaching techniques, program strategies,     and client engagement tools.</li></ul><ul><li>Resource     Sharing: Exchange up-to-date information on local community resources,     financial products, and social services that support     low-to-moderate-income residents.</li></ul><ul><li>Peer     Support &amp; Collaboration: Build professional connections, troubleshoot     client challenges with fellow practitioners, and reduce isolation among     coaches across non-profit, housing, and social service agencies.</li></ul><ul><li>Skill     Building: Stay informed on emerging trends in financial empowerment,     consumer protection, and state-level economic resources.</li></ul><p> Registration Required.</p><br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://register.gotowebinar.com/register/832114149467688032\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        Service Provider      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">WSAC Financial Aid Webinar</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday December 1, 2026 5:30 PM - 6:30 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          This session is offered in English and Spanish / esta presentación está disponible en inglés y español.<br><br>Join the 12th Year Campaign to learn more about financial aid and take your first step creating your StudentAid.gov account (FSA ID) or WASFA account at this event.  Please only use your initials instead of your full first and last name when you register. <br><br> Únase a la campaña del duodécimo año para obtener más información sobre la ayuda financiera y dé el primer paso para crear su FSA ID o cuenta WASFA en este evento.  Utilice únicamente sus iniciales en lugar de su nombre y apellido cuando se registre.  <br><br>Registration required.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://wsac-wa-gov.zoom.us/meeting/register/OmW0Qm5DT6G5uLAQo5tfgQ#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-providers  event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Washington State Health Care Authority: Trauma-informed Care for Career Services Series - Part 2</span><span class=\"ml-3\"> Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\"></span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday December 15, 2026 8:30 AM - 10:00 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          The Washington State Health Care Authority (HCA) Foundational Community Supports (FCS) team invite you to join them and Rutgers Department of Psychiatric Rehabilitation and Counseling Professions for a four-part series on Trauma-Informed Care (TIC).<br>  <br>This four-part webinar series will explore how trauma can affect a person’s experience with career services, looking for work, and being successful on the job. We’ll talk about what trauma can look like in everyday interactions and how providers can respond in ways that build trust, safety, and connection.<br><br>The series will focus on practical strategies that providers can use in supported employment, including job development, placement, coaching, and retention. We’ll also look at how trauma can affect workplace skills, communication, stress, and job success. Participants will be introduced to tools such as cognitive restructuring that can help individuals work through thoughts and challenges that may get in the way of their employment goals. Attendees will leave each webinar with practical ideas they can use with the people they support.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://rutgers.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_aMT_WnpBST2AsgC3HQkwpA#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         Service Providers      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-provider event-free event-hybrid\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\"> Washington Financial Coaching Network</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Hybrid</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday December 23, 2026 2:00 PM - 3:00 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          A peer-learningcommunity for financial coaches and navigators across the state. Held on the4th Wednesday of each month, the meeting provides a collaborative space to:<ul><li>Share     Best Practices: Discuss effective coaching techniques, program strategies,     and client engagement tools.</li></ul><ul><li>Resource     Sharing: Exchange up-to-date information on local community resources,     financial products, and social services that support     low-to-moderate-income residents.</li></ul><ul><li>Peer     Support &amp; Collaboration: Build professional connections, troubleshoot     client challenges with fellow practitioners, and reduce isolation among     coaches across non-profit, housing, and social service agencies.</li></ul><ul><li>Skill     Building: Stay informed on emerging trends in financial empowerment,     consumer protection, and state-level economic resources.</li></ul><p> Registration Required.</p><br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://register.gotowebinar.com/register/832114149467688032\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        Service Provider      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-providers  event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Washington State Health Care Authority: Trauma-informed Care for Career Services Series - Part 3</span><span class=\"ml-3\"> Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\"></span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday January 19, 2027 8:30 AM - 10:00 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          The Washington State Health Care Authority (HCA) Foundational Community Supports (FCS) team invite you to join them and Rutgers Department of Psychiatric Rehabilitation and Counseling Professions for a four-part series on Trauma-Informed Care (TIC).<br>  <br>This four-part webinar series will explore how trauma can affect a person’s experience with career services, looking for work, and being successful on the job. We’ll talk about what trauma can look like in everyday interactions and how providers can respond in ways that build trust, safety, and connection.<br><br>The series will focus on practical strategies that providers can use in supported employment, including job development, placement, coaching, and retention. We’ll also look at how trauma can affect workplace skills, communication, stress, and job success. Participants will be introduced to tools such as cognitive restructuring that can help individuals work through thoughts and challenges that may get in the way of their employment goals. Attendees will leave each webinar with practical ideas they can use with the people they support.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://rutgers.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_aMT_WnpBST2AsgC3HQkwpA#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         Service Providers      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-provider event-free event-hybrid\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\"> Washington Financial Coaching Network</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Hybrid</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday January 27, 2027 2:00 PM - 3:00 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          A peer-learningcommunity for financial coaches and navigators across the state. Held on the4th Wednesday of each month, the meeting provides a collaborative space to:<ul><li>Share     Best Practices: Discuss effective coaching techniques, program strategies,     and client engagement tools.</li></ul><ul><li>Resource     Sharing: Exchange up-to-date information on local community resources,     financial products, and social services that support     low-to-moderate-income residents.</li></ul><ul><li>Peer     Support &amp; Collaboration: Build professional connections, troubleshoot     client challenges with fellow practitioners, and reduce isolation among     coaches across non-profit, housing, and social service agencies.</li></ul><ul><li>Skill     Building: Stay informed on emerging trends in financial empowerment,     consumer protection, and state-level economic resources.</li></ul><p> Registration Required.</p><br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://register.gotowebinar.com/register/832114149467688032\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        Service Provider      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-providers  event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Washington State Health Care Authority: Trauma-informed Care for Career Services Series - Part 4</span><span class=\"ml-3\"> Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\"></span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday February 16, 2027 8:30 AM - 10:00 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          The Washington State Health Care Authority (HCA) Foundational Community Supports (FCS) team invite you to join them and Rutgers Department of Psychiatric Rehabilitation and Counseling Professions for a four-part series on Trauma-Informed Care (TIC).<br>  <br>This four-part webinar series will explore how trauma can affect a person’s experience with career services, looking for work, and being successful on the job. We’ll talk about what trauma can look like in everyday interactions and how providers can respond in ways that build trust, safety, and connection.<br><br>The series will focus on practical strategies that providers can use in supported employment, including job development, placement, coaching, and retention. We’ll also look at how trauma can affect workplace skills, communication, stress, and job success. Participants will be introduced to tools such as cognitive restructuring that can help individuals work through thoughts and challenges that may get in the way of their employment goals. Attendees will leave each webinar with practical ideas they can use with the people they support.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://rutgers.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_aMT_WnpBST2AsgC3HQkwpA#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audi